A1  Triangle device on each family: Koide's ratio Q = sum m / (sum sqrt m)^2  (2/3 means the sqrt-mass point sits at 45 deg)
   charged leptons  Q = 0.666664 +- 0.000005   (2/3 = 0.666667)  off by 0.4 sigma
   up quarks        Q = 0.848809 +- 0.000252   (2/3 = 0.666667)  off by 723.7 sigma
   down quarks      Q = 0.731848 +- 0.000662   (2/3 = 0.666667)  off by 98.5 sigma

A2  Where the middle generation sits on the straight line of the flat triangle: f = ln(m2/m1) / ln(m3/m1)
   charged leptons  f = 0.6539
   up quarks        f = 0.5651
   down quarks      f = 0.4393
   spread 0.215 -> shared position KILLED

