   down quarks      steps    19.77,    45.06   peels 0.9037, 0.9566   past the wall: [np.True_, np.True_]

C  Bosons.  Derived identity first: peel of mZ/mW = (1 - cos thW)/(1 + cos thW) = tan^2(thW/2) (on-shell cos thW = mW/mZ)
   mZ/mW = 1.134707  peel 0.063103  tan^2(thW/2) = 0.063103  (thW = 28.202 deg, sin^2 = 0.22334)
C2  Higgs as the straight midpoint (geometric mean) of Z and top: kill if off by more than 3 sigma
   sqrt(mZ mt) = 125455.30 MeV vs mH = 125130 MeV: off 0.260% = 2.2 sigma -> survives
   look-elsewhere: real triples within 0.3%: 1 ; random masses over the same span give >= that 27.2% of the time

